          <s1auxsar:standAloneProductInformation>
            <s1auxsar:auxProductType>AUX_PP1</s1auxsar:auxProductType>
            <s1auxsar:validity>2024-12-04T00:00:00.000000</s1auxsar:validity>
            <s1auxsar:generation>2025-05-15T13:24:06.000000</s1auxsar:generation>
            <s1auxsar:instrumentConfigurationId>2</s1auxsar:instrumentConfigurationId>
            <s1auxsar:changeDescription><![CDATA[Description

Activation of RFI mitigation on EW and IW mode using the strategy BasedOnNoiseMeasurements

Introduction of the new field geodeticElevationAnglesFlag in slcProcParams requiered for IPF 003.92. For S1C it is set to true <geodeticElevationAnglesFlag>true</geodeticElevationAnglesFlag>, for all the modes, meaning that the elevation angle will be computed with the geodetic reference. This field is ignored by IPF 003.91. It will be only considered in the processing wihen IPF 003.92 will be deployed and used.

This specific ADF applies for S1C RDB2.

Reference

RDBADF-206]]></s1auxsar:changeDescription>
          </s1auxsar:standAloneProductInformation>
        </xmlData>
